255
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:57,580
a step further, with white fish,

256
00:08:57,980 --> 00:08:59,840
mix lots of minced garlic into ssamjang...

257
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,650
- with a dash of sesame oil... - That...

258
00:09:01,650 --> 00:09:04,650
Pairing that with white fish is an absolute match made in heaven.

259
00:09:04,750 --> 00:09:06,750
It beats chojang hands down.

260
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:08,050
You should definitely try it sometime.

261
00:09:08,390 --> 00:09:10,920
What about that one? The food she wants to bring back...

262
00:09:11,090 --> 00:09:13,490
- to her home country, Japan? - Ramen?

263
00:09:13,490 --> 00:09:15,190
If it were ramen, she'd already have it back home.

264
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:16,630
Isn't it cold noodles?

265
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:18,930
- Pyeongyang-style Cold Noodles. - Milmyeon.

266
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,260
- No. - Makguksu.

267
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:22,170
cold soy milk noodle soup.

268
00:09:22,630 --> 00:09:23,870
Yes, cold soy milk noodle soup.

269
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,840
Right. Cold soy milk noodle soup.

270
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:28,940
(She wants to take cold soy milk noodle soup to Japan.)

271
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:31,680
I've been to every famous spot in Seoul.

272
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:32,980
Did you go to that one place in Yeouido too?

273
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:34,650
- I did. - The real deal.

274
00:09:34,710 --> 00:09:36,150
I waited in line. It was the first food in my life...

275
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:38,720
that made me take a bus in Korea.

276
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:39,920
(Unstoppable love for cold soy milk noodle soup)

277
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:42,090
- Yes, I rode a bus. - Wait a second,

278
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:44,860
how do you eat your cold soy milk noodle soup? With sugar or salt?

279
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:48,560
(With sugar or salt? That is the question.)

280
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:50,560
I don't put anything in it.

281
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:52,430
- That's not easy. - With kimchi?

282
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,170
Kimchi, or just plain as it is.

283
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:56,500
- She's an absolute purist. - She's for real.

284
00:09:56,570 --> 00:09:59,340
Shaving some Truffle over it is really tasty too.

285
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:00,440
- That is... - My gosh.

286
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:02,070
Truffle isn't just lying around everywhere...

287
00:10:02,270 --> 00:10:03,370
Only at your house, man.

288
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:05,940
No, I didn't eat it at home, but at a Fine Dining restaurant...

289
00:10:06,010 --> 00:10:07,450
They shaved Truffle over cold soy milk noodle soup,

290
00:10:07,510 --> 00:10:08,880
and it was amazing.

291
00:10:08,950 --> 00:10:10,550
Well, I guess I'll visit Fine Dining in my next life.

292
00:10:10,550 --> 00:10:13,120
(Teasing him)

293
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:16,490
Seeing the tables of our three families like this,

294
00:10:16,490 --> 00:10:17,790
it makes me feel like we've gotten a lot closer.

295
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:19,060
- I know. - It feels that way.

296
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,120
Totally, totally.

297
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:22,860
We told everyone to wear something red today, so...

298
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,560
- It is red. - Right.

299
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,900
Hot sauce inside a bottle.

300
00:10:27,630 --> 00:10:29,930
- My spicy look is always black. - Right, right.

301
00:10:30,230 --> 00:10:31,800
Hitomi and Woonhak too.

302
00:10:32,070 --> 00:10:33,570
- Jaemin and Chenle too. - They look good in red.

303
00:10:33,770 --> 00:10:36,170
The shade of red really suits both of them.

304
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:39,010
- Minnie doesn't have any. - It's a South American style.

305
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:42,280
(A pop of red with a hip scarf)

306
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,580
- As an accent. - An accent...

307
00:10:43,650 --> 00:10:45,580
- Time for belly dancing. - Belly dance.

308
00:10:46,950 --> 00:10:49,350
(Starting as hot as the passionate color)

309
00:10:49,850 --> 00:10:51,760
So today's topic we prepared is...

310
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:55,130
what the whole world goes crazy for. Ta-da, the Red Flavor!

311
00:10:55,330 --> 00:10:57,060
- Red Flavor. - That's right.

312
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,460
(What the world goes crazy for)

313
00:10:59,630 --> 00:11:01,070
(From global spice)

314
00:11:01,070 --> 00:11:03,370
(From global spice to fiery K-red flavor)

315
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:05,470
(Let us fire up today's spicy talk.)

316
00:11:07,410 --> 00:11:09,540
How spicy flavors differ...

317
00:11:09,610 --> 00:11:13,240
- from country to country... - Korean spicy flavor...

318
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:16,610
is pretty complex, isn't it? It's spicy, sweet, and savory...

319
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:18,980
- all mixed together. - Right.

320
00:11:19,050 --> 00:11:20,820
- Isn't kimchi the closest? - Pretty much, yes.

321
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:21,890
Right, right.

322
00:11:21,990 --> 00:11:23,190
There are so many kinds of spicy flavors.

323
00:11:23,250 --> 00:11:26,220
Most people in Korea only know mala.

324
00:11:26,290 --> 00:11:29,060
Mala is just one of many kinds of spiciness.

325
00:11:29,130 --> 00:11:31,100
- "Ma" means numbing... - Numbing.

326
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:33,760
That is what it means, and "la" means spicy...

327
00:11:33,930 --> 00:11:35,430
There's Xiang La, and Xiang La...

328
00:11:35,430 --> 00:11:37,200
- Right. - And...

329
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:38,940
(2. Xiang ma: Fragrant and numbing)

330
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,240
(4. Gan la: Stir-fried or dried)

331
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:41,340
(5. Hong la: Rich and deep spice of chili oil)

332
00:11:41,410 --> 00:11:42,640
(The unstoppable spicy Lele train)

333
00:11:42,710 --> 00:11:44,640
There are so many spicy dishes in China.

334
00:11:44,710 --> 00:11:47,550
- Of course. - Malatang, and mala xiang guo.

335
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:48,710
And one that I really loved,

336
00:11:48,710 --> 00:11:49,780
- Shuizhu Roupian. - Shuizhu Rou?

337
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:51,420
It's called Shuizhu Rou...

338
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:56,120
You boil meat, and the broth is really spicy.

339
00:11:56,650 --> 00:11:59,490
It really sounds like the ultimate spicy dish.

340
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:01,660
When ordering Thai food, you can customize it...

341
00:12:01,730 --> 00:12:03,330
in a lot of detail.

342
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:04,730
- In our country... - Really?

343
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,400
Starting from how many chili peppers to put in,

344
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:09,270
spicy or not spicy, and all kinds of other things...

345
00:12:09,330 --> 00:12:10,600
You can choose every detail.

346
00:12:11,270 --> 00:12:12,870
Thailand is serious about spicy food too.

347
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,070
Totally serious.

348
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:16,170
Still, Japan has spicy dishes too, right?

349
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,780
Yes, that is right. It is not something we eat every day,

350
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:21,910
but do you know the classic Wasabi or Shichimi?

351
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:24,080
- Shichimi. There are seven... - Right.

352
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,250
- various... - That's right.

353
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:28,290
I like it a lot, so when I visited Kyoto,

354
00:12:28,350 --> 00:12:30,050
there was ice cream made with Shichimi.

355
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:32,320
- I wonder what it is like. - It is really delicious.

356
00:12:32,390 --> 00:12:35,060
At first, it tastes like milk, but at the end, it has a slight...

357
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:36,130
Tangy kick?

358
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:38,530
A kick that comes through like that.

359
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,730
We have tried Som Tum ice cream too.

360
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:42,400
- Som Tum ice cream? - Yes.

361
00:12:42,870 --> 00:12:44,340
- How do you eat that? - As an ice cream?

362
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:48,010
- They make it like a sorbet. - Like a sorbet?

363
00:12:48,110 --> 00:12:51,310
- But it is really so delicious. - That is amazing.

364
00:12:51,610 --> 00:12:54,010
When you want to say, "Make it a little spicy,"

365
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:58,080
- how should you phrase it? - "Spicy" is "Phet."

366
00:12:58,150 --> 00:12:59,450
A little spicy, please.

367
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,620
- Phet noi ha. - Phet noi ha.

368
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:01,920
(A Thai Quartet)

369
00:13:02,090 --> 00:13:03,950
- A little spicy, please. - Men say "khrap."

370
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:05,660
- Yes, a little spicy, please. - Khrap.

371
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:07,990
- Khrap. - Your pronunciation is good.

372
00:13:08,090 --> 00:13:10,690
Or if you want to ask for it not spicy at all, say, "My Pet."

373
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:13,030
My Pet. I should memorize that.

374
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,500
Minnie sounds a bit different...

375
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,870
when speaking Thai compared to Korean.

376
00:13:16,930 --> 00:13:18,970
- Really? - Isn't everyone kind of like that?

377
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:21,670
- It does change. - It is different?

378
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:23,940
Wait, what?

379
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:26,140
- You sound so cool speaking Thai. - No, no.

380
00:13:26,210 --> 00:13:27,310
So bold and fearless.

381
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:29,050
(Full-on Chinese baritone voice)

382
00:13:29,910 --> 00:13:31,850
What is this, acting all cool. Why are you showing off?

383
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,780
Everyone acts so cool.

384
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:35,520
(Deadly charm powered by their native tongue)

385
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:36,850
Young people nowadays...

386
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:38,720
have that whole spice pride thing, don't they?

387
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:40,190
The spiciness in each country...

388
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:42,260
- is a little different. - That is true.

389
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:45,000
For example, I handle Chinese spiciness really well.

390
00:13:45,730 --> 00:13:47,900
Korean spiciness is hard for me, though.

391
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:50,070
Honestly, Korean spicy food is a bit tough for me too.

392
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:51,740
China and Thailand are similar...

393
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,200
in that it hits hard for a moment,

394
00:13:53,270 --> 00:13:55,440
hurts, and then goes away in 5 to 10 minutes.

395
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:57,680
However, Korean spice lingers for so long,

396
00:13:57,780 --> 00:13:59,110
and your trips to the bathroom linger too.

397
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:00,910
(Suddenly sharing TMI)

398
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:02,080
Right, right.

399
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:05,380
In Thailand, when you eat Som Tum, people are divided...

400
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:08,720
by how many chili peppers they put in.

401
00:14:08,790 --> 00:14:11,520
- How many usually? - I put in about 2 or 3,

402
00:14:11,690 --> 00:14:14,960
- but BamBam puts in as many as ten. - Ten?

403
00:14:15,030 --> 00:14:16,330
That is intense.

404
00:14:16,390 --> 00:14:17,900
Two or three is spicy enough,

405
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,600
but he is on another level.

406
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:21,830
Come on. But I like it. It is just really good.

407
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:23,300
- Totally. - Honestly, in our country,

408
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,840
we take spice pride, including myself,

409
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:26,440
- pretty seriously, you know? - That is true.

410
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,770
Well, Woonhak,

411
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,840
you are used to vegetables now.

412
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:31,280
Yes, I am a bit more familiar with them now.

413
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:33,540
Dipping a chili pepper in Ssamjang with white rice.

414
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:36,010
- I have not tried that yet. - You have not?

415
00:14:36,010 --> 00:14:37,380
I heard that is... That is the real...

416
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:40,780
- The real deal, though. - We should ask that...

417
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,320
- to our Chamisul Original guy. - Yes, absolutely.

418
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:43,850
What is the dish that made you think...

419
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,220
"I am fully Korean now"?

420
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,860
- Rice noodles... - What is that?

421
00:14:47,930 --> 00:14:49,230
Is that red?

422
00:14:49,590 --> 00:14:51,460
- It's fire. - Not that, the cap.

423
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,600
What color is the cap?

424
00:14:53,130 --> 00:14:55,370
The cap? Isn't the cap red?

425
00:14:55,430 --> 00:14:56,700
Chamisul Original.

426
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:58,970
Sorry, sorry.

427
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:00,600
Since today's theme is spicy flavor...

428
00:15:00,670 --> 00:15:02,740
- Chamisul Original Jaemin. - Too bad.

429
00:15:03,070 --> 00:15:05,740
Here is the thing. With kimchi, you know...

430
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:07,280
With kimchi.

431
00:15:07,910 --> 00:15:09,180
There is aged kimchi, right?

432
00:15:09,550 --> 00:15:12,080
I bought it and put it in the fridge,

433
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,480
and when you live alone...

434
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,520
sometimes you forget about it.

435
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,990
- True. - When you open that container...

436
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:19,660
The smell.

437
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:22,460
The smell.

438
00:15:24,030 --> 00:15:26,330
- There is that kind of kimchi. - Right, totally, there is.

439
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:29,200
You put some on a small plate with chopsticks,

440
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,200
and then you take a shot.

441
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,470
(Then you take a shot.)

442
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:32,570
(I love it.)

443
00:15:33,270 --> 00:15:35,110
Wait. Jaemin, does that mean...

444
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:37,070
- you have kimchi with drinks? - Yes.

445
00:15:37,370 --> 00:15:39,140
Impressive. You are like an old man...

446
00:15:39,210 --> 00:15:42,150
- The ultimate old-school gentleman. - A changing of the guard, right?

447
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:43,450
Did you feel that just now?

448
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,480
So is there any spicy dish...

449
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:49,450
that caught you completely off guard after coming to Korea?

450
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:53,060
- A memorable one? - As a trainee, Fire Chicken...

451
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:57,060
- Fire Chicken. Yes. - It was so spicy and painful...

452
00:15:57,090 --> 00:15:59,760
- yet you keep craving it. - Right. It's so good.

453
00:15:59,830 --> 00:16:01,730
- It has that good kind of heat. - When you are a trainee,

454
00:16:01,730 --> 00:16:03,600
those noodles taste twice as good.

455
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:07,040
After practice, on your way home, sneaking into a convenience store...

456
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:08,970
and making a bowl... Nothing beats it.

457
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:12,340
That is so true, because after I debuted,

458
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:14,450
- I never had it again. - Really?

459
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:16,050
You need Truffle sprinkled on it now.

460
00:16:16,110 --> 00:16:19,420
You need shaved Truffle.

461
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:21,520
You cannot live without Truffle now...

462
00:16:21,590 --> 00:16:22,990
His tastes got fancy.

463
00:16:23,450 --> 00:16:24,590
Since you can't live without Truffle...

464
00:16:25,790 --> 00:16:28,690
- What about you, BamBam? - For me, Dongdaemun tteokbokki.

465
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:31,430
I was also a trainee back then.

466
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,100
We decided to go and eat Dongdaemun tteokbokki,

467
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:37,500
and there were spice levels ranging from mildest to spiciest.

468
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:41,440
I thought, "How spicy could it be?" and ordered the hottest one.

469
00:16:42,270 --> 00:16:45,580
After 5 to 10 minutes of eating,

470
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:48,210
yes, it killed me.

471
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:50,750
My lips doubled in size. They are already big, so...

472
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:53,680
I think it was the spiciest food I've had in Korea.

473
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:54,820
(Just thinking of it makes him feel the spiciness)

474
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:57,250
When I was a trainee,

475
00:16:57,320 --> 00:17:00,060
there were only specific restaurants we could go to.

476
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,690
- Right. - Right?

477
00:17:01,690 --> 00:17:03,930
- Yes, exactly. - And one place served...

478
00:17:03,990 --> 00:17:06,230
authentic Korean food.

479
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:09,970
Back then, both JYP and Cube went to the restaurant between them.

480
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:12,340
- We all went to the same one. - I know that place.

481
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,500
You do?

482
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:14,570
(Woonhak from a different company knows that place?)

483
00:17:14,770 --> 00:17:17,240
- Wasn't it called Alley Restaurant? - Yes.

484
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:20,440
- Oh, right, right. - It must be famous among trainees.

485
00:17:20,510 --> 00:17:21,750
I just remembered the owner said...

486
00:17:22,210 --> 00:17:24,310
"BamBam used to eat so much of my food back then."

487
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:25,420
She literally told me that.

488
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:27,650
- It just popped into my head. - I really did eat a lot.

489
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:30,420
(Bambam's trace on the top shelf)

490
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:32,260
Their rich soybean paste stew is amazing.

491
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,320
It is really delicious.

492
00:17:33,490 --> 00:17:35,760
Everything was red, though.

493
00:17:37,530 --> 00:17:40,200
Kimchi stew, kimchi fried rice...

494
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:41,730
I was so shocked that day...

495
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:44,400
- I only ate rice and seaweed. - Really?

496
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:46,300
Yes, everything was too red.

497
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,940
All right, then, I think it is about time...

498
00:17:50,010 --> 00:17:52,380
we see what kind of spice our guest brought.

499
00:17:52,510 --> 00:17:55,710
(Great anticipation for the spicy dish)

500
00:17:55,910 --> 00:17:58,480
The one showing off spicy flavor today...

501
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,950
is our newest member, Minnie.

502
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:01,850
(The star of today's recipe is Minnie.)

503
00:18:01,850 --> 00:18:03,150
- Let's see. - I can't wait.

504
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,250
- I'm excited. - Will it have...

505
00:18:04,390 --> 00:18:06,460
- Thailand's spicy kick? - I love that.

506
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:07,830
But you know, she really cannot cook, right?

507
00:18:07,890 --> 00:18:10,390
- My goodness. - Seriously. Seriously.

508
